course: dictionary
lesson: 4909
title: Picturing and guessing with imagine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To imagine something is to picture it in your mind, even when it is not there. «Imagine a purple cow.» You can see it in your head, and no real cow is needed.
explain: Imagine can also mean to guess or think that something is true. «I imagine you are tired.» The speaker is not completely sure, but thinks it is likely. Swap in guess or think: «I guess you are tired» still makes sense.
explain: Imagine can mean to think you see or hear something when it is not real. «Children often hear bits of grown-up money talk and imagine the worst.» They make up scary ideas that may not be true, and asking a parent is usually better than guessing.
fact: Imagine is a verb. Its other forms are imagines, imagined and imagining.
fact: To imagine means to picture something in your mind, such as «Imagine a purple cow.»
fact: To imagine can also mean to guess or think that something is true, such as «I imagine you are tired.»
fact: «Imagined» can mean you thought you saw or heard something that was not real.
fact: A good check is to swap in picture, guess or think. If the sentence still makes sense, imagine is probably the right meaning.
exercise: «Imagine a purple cow.» What does imagine mean here? | To count coins quickly | *To picture something in your mind | To eat slowly | To cross a road safely
exercise: «I imagine you are tired.» In this sentence, imagine means: | To forget a rule | To move quickly | To shout loudly | *To guess or think that something is true
exercise: «Imagine 3 bags with 4 apples in each.» How many apples are there in all? | *12 | 7 | 1 | 34
test: «Imagine your friend knocks a vase off the teacher's desk, and the teacher asks the class who did it.» Which word in this sentence tells you to picture a scene? | *Imagine | Class | Knocks | Teacher
test: Tom woke up and imagined he heard a dog barking, but the house was silent. What does imagined mean here? | Fed the dog | Heard a real dog outside | Forgot about the dog | *Thought he heard something that was not real
exam: «A thought experiment is an imagined situation used to test ideas.» In this sentence, imagined means: | Broken into pieces | *Made up in the mind, not something that really happened | Real and measured in a lab | Painted in bright colours
